ARM64 port (roadmap step 14) — step by step
============================================

Portable code stays in kernel/, mm/, fs/. This directory is CPU-specific only.

Done:
  - Hello on PL011 (QEMU virt)
  - Embedded virt.dtb, FDT /memory + host unit test
  - EL1 vector table + sync fault print
  - PMM bitmap (2 GiB frame index space)
  - EL1 MMU: TTBR0 identity, 1 GiB blocks (low MMIO + RAM bank)
  - GICv2 @ 0x08000000 + architected timer (1 kHz, IRQ vector @ 0x280)
  - Slab kheap (≤1 KiB) + kprintf → PL011; pmm_alloc/free
  - EL0 + SVC @ 0x400; write(64) + uaccess; sync_el0 saves x0–x5/x8
  - Alpine aarch64 musl-dev fetch; ELF64 load @ 0x40400000; static musl hello test
  - `make ARCH=arm64 test` greps `musl hello from MyOS`

Next (14b):
  - Fix EL0 data mapping (full musl crt / GOT — docs/gaps.md)
  - initramfs + exec from cpio; Alpine aarch64 busybox.static as /init
  - Grow syscall set (open, read, brk, mmap, exit_group, …)

